menu "Knob time bridge"

config KNOB_TIME_BOOT_SYNC_MS
    int "Boot NTP fix window (ms)"
    default 20000
    range 5000 120000
    help
        How long the boot arm task waits for the first SNTP fix
        (clock_sync_time_from_ntp with CLOCK_NTP_SERVER) before giving
        up on a trusted fix. After the window the glass arms on the
        NVS snapshot as "last known" (or stays "no time") and a late fix
        re-bakes the STATIC current phase.

config KNOB_TZ
    string "POSIX TZ string for the glass caption (e.g. CET-1CEST,M3.5.0/2,M10.5.0/3)"
    default "UTC0"
    help
        The caption clock formats the instant through this TZ so the
        knob and the clocks agree on glass. Interim home until the
        shared clock_tz settings screen lands (P2 retires this key);
        an invalid POSIX string makes newlib fall back to UTC.

config KNOB_TIME_USE_TEST_EPOCH
    bool "Bench: frozen KNOB_MOON_TEST_EPOCH as now (no SNTP)"
    default n
    help
        Bench builds only: the boot arm treats KNOB_MOON_TEST_EPOCH as
        a trusted instant and never starts SNTP -- this is what keeps
        the K7b/K7c frozen-epoch verifications (blood tint at the
        2025-03-14 eclipse, the single midnight re-bake) reproducible.
        Production leaves this n: SNTP truth or "no time".

endmenu
